  "summary": "Ira Frederick Aldridge (July 24, 1807 – August 7, 1867) was an American-born British actor, playwright, and theatre manager, known for his portrayal of Shakespearean characters. James Hewlett and Aldridge are regarded as the first Black American tragedians.\nBorn in New York City, Aldridge's first professional acting experience was in the early 1820s with the African Grove Theatre troupe.",
